# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): the class bitmap words are vstd
# `PAtomicU64`s, proved over vstd's operations (no seam here). What stays
# trusted is the fork slot, `api::FORK_SIGMASK`, a `core` `AtomicU64`:
# its one write is `api::save_sigmask`'s raw `store`, through no
# permission (tests/loom/tests/access.rs), and that the permission
# `api::resume::axiom_fork_resumed` mints holds the stored mask is that
# axiom's premise; no model covers it. Its accesses are `Relaxed`,
# ordered by the allocator's locks, which the slot's writer and reader
# both hold (`api::FORK_SIGMASK`).
# Kani runs the wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
load_fork_slot	atomics primitive	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::word_load_fork_slot; not checked: that the permission's value is the slot's last write, `api::resume::axiom_fork_resumed`'s premise, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only (`api::save_sigmask`'s raw `store` is the slot's one write), and that `fork_slot_id` is the slot's identity, ghost; no model covers the slot)	contract 1964652950, body 1486267455
